  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stakeholder engagement and training local verifiers of livestock predation: A project to reduce.human-puma conflicts in Chile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to diminish and prevent livestock predation by pumas in two eco-regions (tropical Andes and temperate forest) of Chile to reduce the justification for their legal or illegal retaliatory killing. Project activities include one set of workshops for local stakeholders in developing and implementing a predation verification system to detect puma predation on livestock and discriminate such events from other causes of livestock loss. A second set of workshops will be directed to livestock owners in selecting, designing and implementing non-lethal interventions based on cost-efficient design, scientific effectiveness, and social acceptability.</narrative>
  </description>
